# abc_ofs_canonicalize.patch — registers the `abc_ofs` source in the mandatory door.
#
# Apply inside archdisc-Models:   git apply scripts/abc_ofs_canonicalize.patch
# (that checkout has no remote; it is a local repo, so this is a local commit)
#
# NOT INSTALLED BY THIS BRANCH, and the reason is mechanical rather than a
# judgement call: this work ran inside an isolated Forge worktree whose
# harness REFUSES writes into the archdisc-Models checkout. scripts/
# abc_ofs_corpus.py therefore imports the real canonicalize_dataset and
# registers the same adapter IN MEMORY, so the door that produced the
# measured corpus is byte-for-byte the door this patch modifies -- there is
# no second pipeline, and installing this patch changes nothing about the
# rows, only who drives it.
#
# scripts/abc_ofs_adapter.py must be importable (add the Forge scripts/ dir
# to PYTHONPATH, or copy that one file next to canonicalize_dataset.py).

--- a/scripts/canonicalize_dataset.py
